Let me analyze `removeYamlPath` for bugs:

The loop:
```dart
for (var depth = segments.length - 1; depth >= 0; depth--) {
    final keyLine = foundAt[depth];
    final end = _blockEnd(lines, keyLine, depth);
    lines.removeRange(keyLine, end);
    // An emptied ancestor block: the parent key line now carries no body.
    if (depth > 0) {
      final parentLine = foundAt[depth - 1];
      if (_blockEnd(lines, parentLine, depth - 1) == parentLine + 1) {
        continue; // loop's next iteration removes the emptied parent
      }
      break;
    }
```

Deepest-first removal: removes leaf block; then checks if parent block becomes empty — if so, continue to next iteration which removes the parent (at depth-1), etc.

Note: `foundAt[depth - 1]` — the parent line index. After removing the child block (which is AFTER the parent line), the parent index stays valid. Good.

But wait — the `break` in the `else` branch: if the parent is NOT empty, we break. But the loop decrements depth anyway... no, break exits. OK.

